    {
      "id": "function:yosoi::locators::LocateResult::try_new_with_regions",
      "publicPath": "yosoi::locators::LocateResult::try_new_with_regions",
      "title": "yosoi::locators::LocateResult::try_new_with_regions",
      "kind": "function",
      "signature": "pub fn try_new_with_regions(document_id: yosoi::DocumentId, regions: Vec<yosoi::locators::RegionLineage>, findings: Vec<yosoi::locators::Finding>) -> Result<Self, LocateResultError>",
      "docs": "Creates a result with explicit owned matched regions and findings.\n\nAt least one collection must be nonempty. Region lineage must be unique;\nfindings must belong to `document_id`, have strictly increasing order,\nand refer only to parent lineage present in `regions`. Returns\n[`LocateResultError`] for violations. This validates structure, not the\ntruth of completeness claims or coordinates against a live document.",
